<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 24 April, from 1184 BCE to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/troy" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/troy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1184 BCE <span class="tih-ago">3,209 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Troy falls, according to ancient Greek reckoning</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Greek chronographers, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eratosthenes">Eratosthenes</a>, dated the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a> to 1184 BCE, and later writers placed it in late April. The legend, told in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virgil">Virgil</a>, shaped European literature for millennia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/934">934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,092 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Abbasid caliph al-Qahir is deposed and blinded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Al-Qahir, the nineteenth Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, was deposed and blinded, and his nephew al-Radi succeeded him. Al-Radi's reign marked the end of the caliph's political power and the rise of military strongmen competing for the title of amir al-umara.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1547">1547 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">479 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles V defeats the Schmalkaldic League at Mühlberg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-alvarez-de-toledo-3rd-duke-of-alba">Duke of Alba</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> near Mühlberg, surprised the Protestant army of Elector John Frederick I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and captured the elector. The battle decided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-war">Schmalkaldic War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-muhlberg">Battle of Mühlberg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-league">Schmalkaldic League</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1558">1558 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">468 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary, Queen of Scots, marries the Dauphin Francis in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mary, Queen of Scots, married Francis, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dauphin-of-france">Dauphin of France</a> and heir to the French throne, at Notre-Dame de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. Francis became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1559 and, as Mary's husband, was also King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> until his death in 1560.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dauphin-of-france">Dauphin of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1800">1800 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress establishes the Library of Congress</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President John Adams signed the act moving the government to Washington and setting aside $5,000 for books for Congress. The collection became one of the largest libraries in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1877">1877 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Russia declares war on the Ottoman Empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> went to war in support of the Balkan Christians. The peace that followed made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and Montenegro fully independent and created an autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1915">1915 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ottoman authorities arrest Armenian leaders in Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hundreds of Armenian intellectuals and community leaders were rounded up and deported, most later killed. The date marks the start of the Armenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>, in which around a million people died.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Irish rebels launch the Easter Rising in Dublin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Irish Volunteers and the Citizen Army seized the General Post Office and proclaimed an Irish Republic. The Rising was crushed within a week, but the executions that followed turned opinion towards independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1990">1990 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Space shuttle Discovery launches the Hubble Space Telescope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hubble was carried into orbit by Discovery and deployed the next day. A flaw in its mirror was corrected in 1993, after which it transformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 24 April <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-the-silent"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-the-silent.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William the Silent</span><span class="tp">1533–1584</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guglielmo-gonzaga-duke-of-mantua"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guglielmo-gonzaga-duke-of-mantua.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Guglielmo Gonzaga, Duke of Mantua</span><span class="tp">1538–1587</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sebastian-lerdo-de-tejada"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sebastian-lerdo-de-tejada.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sebastián Lerdo de Tejada</span><span class="tp">1823–1889</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philippe-petain"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philippe-petain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philippe Pétain</span><span class="tp">1856–1951</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-sarney"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-sarney.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Sarney</span><span class="tp">b. 1930</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 24 April <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mellitus"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Mellitus</span><span class="tp">d. 624</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/daniel-defoe"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/daniel-defoe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Daniel Defoe</span><span class="tp">c. 1660–1731</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
